# CLI tools manifest — declares the intended per-layer tool set. Versions and
# install mechanisms stay with each installer on purpose (iv-image pins for
# team reproducibility; dotfiles floats at latest) — this file is only the
# "what", not the "how".
#
# Columns (whitespace-separated):
#   layer  base | team | personal | personal-mac
#   tool   command name on PATH
#
# Layers:
#   base      provided by the stock exeuntu image on exe.dev VMs. Informational
#             — exeuntu is exe.dev-managed and can't be checked from here.
#             install.sh may still install these (need-guarded) for macOS and
#             non-exeuntu hosts.
#   team      pinned and installed by iv-image provision-iv.sh on VMs.
#             install.sh also installs duckdb/quarto/tigris/herdr/agentsview and
#             uv/claude/codex (floating) so macOS gets them — a known,
#             intentional overlap. want() skips team tools on IV VMs so the
#             floating copy never shadows provision-iv.sh's pin.
#   personal  dotfiles-only: installed by install.sh, absent from iv-image.
#   personal-mac  like personal, but macOS-only — install.sh skips it on Linux
#             VMs (see the gh/croc note below). Same drift invariants as personal.
#
# Consumers: none yet (installers are still imperative); checked by
# diff-provisioning.sh (team ⊆ provision-iv.sh, personal/personal-mac ⊆
# install.sh, personal ∩ provision-iv.sh = ∅).

# exeuntu-provided (asserted in-repo: jq per iv-image setup-mcp.sh; git/curl
# required by provision-iv.sh before it installs anything)
# personal-mac: installed on macOS only. Measured 2026-07-29 as unused on dev
# VMs — gh is unauthenticated there (git uses the exe.dev integration proxy)
# and croc is ad-hoc with no state. 60 MB/VM.

base git
base curl
base jq
# tailscaled ships in exeuntu (disabled); install.sh only starts/joins it
base tailscale

# iv-image layer (provision-iv.sh)
team duckdb
team quarto
team aws
team tigris
team rclone
team herdr
team agentsview
team shelley
team render-site
team provision-docsite
team gen-llms-txt
team install-cloud-cli
# Agent/Python CLIs: provision-iv.sh installs and version-pins these on VMs, so
# they are team, not personal -- a personal label made install.sh's floating
# copy shadow the pin on IV VMs (want() skips team tools there) while the
# manifest's own `personal ∩ provision-iv.sh = ∅` invariant read as violated.
# install.sh still installs them on macOS, where want() does not skip team.
team uv
team claude
team codex

# personal layer (install.sh)
personal stow
personal zsh
personal starship
personal atuin
personal direnv
personal zoxide
personal archil
personal fnm
personal node
personal bat
personal fzf
personal rg
personal yq
personal-mac gh
personal carapace
personal-mac croc
personal cship
personal snow
personal op
